# Checklist for Publishing to Dart Pub

1. Ensure all code changes are complete and tested.
2. Bump the version in pubspec.yaml (follow semantic versioning).
3. Update CHANGELOG.md (latest entry at the top, summarize changes).
4. Stage and commit all changes (including pubspec.yaml and CHANGELOG.md) with a conventional commit message.
5. Run `dart pub publish --dry-run` to verify package validity and clean git state.
6. Fix any issues or warnings from the dry-run.
7. Run all tests and ensure they pass.
8. Push changes to the remote repository (if applicable).
9. Run `dart pub publish` to publish the package.
10. Verify the package is live on pub.dev.
